  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "If $A={1,3,4,5,7,8,10}$ and $B={2,4,6,8,10,12},$ then $A\u2216B=$",
  "worked_solution": "The set $A\u2216B$ is the set of all elements belonging to $A$ but *not* $B.$ Note that the elements $4,8,10\\in B$ are also in $A,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\u2216B & =A-B \\\\  & ={1,3,4,5,7,8,10}-{2,4,6,8,10,12} \\\\  & ={1,3,5,7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
